[2026-03-14T22:27:21.291Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0129VysynLthoNVxkgaaq7jb","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Linear Clone App - Complete Exploration Summary\n\n### 1. App Directory Name\n**`/repo/apps/LinearClone`** - The main application directory\n\n### 2. Overall Structure\n\nThe app follows a standard React + Redux + Netlify Functions architecture:\n\n**Key directories:**\n- **`src/`** - Frontend React application\n  - **`pages/`** - Top-level page components (routing targets)\n  - **`components/`** - Reusable UI components\n  - **`slices/`** - Redux state management\n- **`netlify/functions/`** - Serverless API endpoints\n- **`tests/`** - Playwright end-to-end tests\n- **`scripts/`** - Database schema and seed utilities\n- **`docs/tests.md`** - Comprehensive test specification document\n- **`playwright.config.ts`** - Test configuration with Replay.io integration\n- **`public/`** - Static assets\n\n### 3. Cycle-Related Components, Pages, and API Endpoints\n\n#### Frontend Pages:\n- **`src/pages/ActiveCycle.tsx`** - Main cycles page at `/team/:teamId/cycles` route\n  - Manages cycle list and detail view toggling\n  - Handles cycle creation via modal\n  - Dispatches Redux actions for cycle fetching and selection\n\n#### Components:\n- **`src/components/CycleList.tsx`** - Displays paginated list of cycles with:\n  - Cycle name, date range, progress bar, issue count\n  - Active cycle highlighting with visual badge\n  - Click to navigate to detail view\n- **`src/components/CycleDetail.tsx`** - Shows detailed cycle view with:\n  - Cycle name, date range, progress statistics (total, completed, in progress, remaining)\n  - Progress bar with percentage\n  - Burndown chart integration\n  - Issue list with grouping (status, priority, assignee, project, label)\n  - Sorting options (priority, created, updated, status)\n  - Status filtering\n  - Bulk issue selection and status updates\n  - All filtering/sorting state stored in Redux\n- **`src/components/CreateCycle.tsx`** - Modal for creating new cycles with:\n  - Name, start date, end date input fields\n  - Form validation (required fields, end date > start date)\n  - Submit button with loading state\n  - Escape key and overlay click to close\n\n#### Redux State Management:\n- **`src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`** - Comprehensive state management:\n  - `CycleSummary` interface: id, name, startDate, endDate, teamId, issueCount, doneCount, inProgressCount, isActive\n  - `CycleIssue` interface: extends Issue with cycleName\n  - `CycleDetail` interface: id, name, startDate, endDate, teamId\n  - `BurndownEntry` interface: date, count\n  - Async thunks:\n    - `fetchCycles(teamId)` - GET `/api/cycles?teamId={teamId}`\n    - `fetchCycleIssues(cycleId)` - GET `/api/cycle-issues?cycleId={cycleId}`\n    - `createCycle(teamId, name, startDate, endDate)` - POST `/api/cycles`\n  - Reducers: setCycleGroupBy, setCycleSortBy, toggleCycleIssueSelection, selectCycleGroupIssues, clearCycleSelection, setSelectedCycleId\n  - State properties: cycles[], loading, error, selectedCycleId, cycleDetail, cycleIssues[], cycleMembers[], burndown[], detailLoading, detailError, groupBy, sortBy, selectedIds[]\n\n#### API Endpoints:\n- **`netlify/functions/cycles.ts`** - GET/POST cycles\n  - **GET** `/api/cycles?teamId={teamId}` - Returns list of cycles with stats, determines active cycle based on current date\n  - **POST** `/api/cycles` - Creates new cycle (requires teamId, name, startDate, endDate)\n  \n- **`netlify/functions/cycle-issues.ts`** - GET cycle details with issues and burndown\n  - **GET** `/api/cycle-issues?cycleId={cycleId}` - Returns cycle info, issues in cycle, team members, and burndown data\n  - Fetches activity log entries where status changed to 'done' for burndown data\n  - Joins with labels, projects, assignees\n\n### 4. Burndown Chart Components\n\n#### Component:\n- **`src/components/BurndownChart.tsx`** - Bar chart visualization showing:\n  - Issues completed per day for the cycle duration\n  - X-axis: All dates from cycle start to end (with smart label skipping for long cycles)\n  - Y-axis: Count of issues (0 to max with even distribution)\n  - Bar heights proportional to issue count\n  - Hover tooltips with date and count\n  - Empty state message when no completions yet\n  - Responsive, scrollable for long date ranges\n\n#### Styling:\n- **`src/components/BurndownChart.css`** - Bar chart styling:\n  - Container with flex layout, overflow scrolling for long date ranges\n  - Y-axis with right-aligned labels\n  - Bars with accent color, smooth height transitions\n  - Rounded bar tops, semi-transparent hover effect\n\n#### Data Flow:\n- BurndownEntry[] fetched from `/api/cycle-issues` endpoint\n- Data points computed from activity log (field='status', new_value='done')\n- Dates within cycle range rendered, others show 0 height\n\n### 5. Existing Test Files (Playwright)\n\nTests follow consistent patterns with helper functions:\n\n**Cycle-Related Tests:**\n- **`tests/cycle-list.spec.ts`** (6 tests)\n  - Renders all cycles with name, date range, progress bar, issue count\n  - Active cycle highlighted with badge and CSS class\n  - Clicking cycle navigates to detail\n  - Empty state when no cycles\n  - Progress bar accuracy\n  - Updates when new cycle created\n  - Switching between cycles in list\n\n- **`tests/cycle-detail.spec.ts`** (8 tests)\n  - Renders cycle name and date range\n  - Shows progress stats (total, completed, in progress, remaining)\n  - Shows progress bar with percentage\n  - Displays filtered issue list\n  - Clicking issue navigates to detail page\n  - Supports grouping by status/priority/assignee\n  - Supports sorting\n  - Supports filtering by status\n  - Supports bulk actions (status change)\n  - Updates stats when issue status changes\n  - Renders correctly for cycle with no issues\n\n- **`tests/create-issue-modal-cycles-dates.spec.ts`** (3+ cycle-related tests)\n  - Cycle dropdown shows team's cycles\n  - Selecting a cycle\n  - Updating cycles when team changes\n\n**Test Pattern:**\n- Login via API and store token in localStorage\n- Use API helpers to fetch teams and cycles\n- Navigate to pages with team/cycle IDs\n- Verify UI with data-testid selectors\n- Test interactions and state changes\n- Timeouts: 30s for page loads, 10s for modals, 15s for interactions\n\n### 6. Test Specification File\n\n**`docs/tests.md`** (48,000+ tokens) contains:\n- Comprehensive test entries for Active Cycle page (section starting line ~1450)\n- Tests cover:\n  - Cycle list rendering and interactions\n  - Cycle detail views\n  - Progress statistics\n  - Burndown chart display\n  - Cycle creation modal\n  - Form validation\n  - Issue list filtering, grouping, sorting, bulk actions\n  - Empty states\n  - Data persistence\n\n**Burndown Chart Test Entries (lines ~1589-1614):**\n- \"Burndown chart displays completion data correctly\"\n- \"Burndown chart shows correct date range\"\n- \"Burndown chart updates in real-time\"\n- \"Burndown chart shows empty state\"\n- \"Burndown chart y-axis scales proportionally\"\n- \"Burndown chart handles long date ranges\"\n\n### 7. Playwright Configuration\n\n**`playwright.config.ts`:**\n- Test timeout: 60 seconds\n- Expect timeout: 10 seconds\n- Fully parallel execution\n- Retry: 0\n- Reporters: Replay.io, JSON results, HTML report\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Action timeout: 15 seconds\n- Uses `@replayio/playwright` for browser recording\n\n### 8. Database Schema and Seed Files\n\n**`scripts/schema.ts`** - Creates PostgreSQL tables:\n- **cycles** table:\n  - id (UUID, PK)\n  - name (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n  - start_date (DATE, NOT NULL)\n  - end_date (DATE, NOT NULL)\n  - team_id (UUID, FK to teams)\n  - status (TEXT, DEFAULT 'active')\n  - Index: idx_cycles_team_id\n\n- **issues** table (extended):\n  - cycle_id (UUID, FK to cycles, nullable)\n  - parent_id (UUID, self-referencing)\n  - Index: idx_issues_cycle_id\n\n- **activity** table - For burndown tracking:\n  - id, issue_id (FK), member_id (FK), action, field, new_value, created_at\n  - Index: idx_activity_issue_id\n\n**`scripts/seed-db.ts`** - Seeds test data:\n- Creates 3 members: Alice (admin), Bob, Carol\n- Creates 2 teams: Engineering (ENG), Design (DES)\n- Creates 1 cycle: \"Sprint 12\" (2026-03-10 to 2026-03-24, active)\n- Creates 8 issues for ENG team with various statuses and assignments\n- Creates 3 issues for DES team\n- Issues assigned to cycle (mostly to Sprint 12)\n- Labels created (Bug, Feature, Improvement, Documentation)\n- Notifications seeded\n\n### 9. Shared UI Components Used in Cycles\n\n#### IssueRow Component (`src/components/IssueRow.tsx`):\n- **Shared across:** Cycle detail, team issues, my issues pages\n- **Features:**\n  - Issue checkbox with selection handling\n  - Status icon (visual indicator by status)\n  - Priority icon\n  - Issue identifier and title\n  - Assignee avatar/initials\n  - Labels display\n  - Due date (if present)\n  - Status dropdown for inline status change\n  - Click to navigate to issue detail\n- **Exports:** STATUS_CONFIG, STATUS_ORDER, StatusIcon, PriorityIcon (used in CycleDetail)\n- **Test IDs:** issue-row-{id}, issue-identifier-{id}, issue-title-{id}, issue-checkbox-{id}, issue-status-btn-{id}\n\n#### Modal Patterns:\n- **CreateCycle.tsx** uses modal overlay pattern:\n  - Fixed overlay with backdrop blur\n  - Centered modal box with shadow\n  - Click outside to close\n  - Escape key handling\n  - Disabled submit button during submission\n\n#### Button Components:\n- All use standard CSS classes with:\n  - Hover states\n  - Disabled states (opacity reduction)\n  - Transition animations (150ms)\n  - Color theming via CSS variables (--color-accent, --color-border, --color-text-*)\n\n#### Dropdown Patterns:\n- Positioned dropdowns with click-outside detection\n- useRef + useEffect for outside click handling\n- Toggle state management\n- Close on selection\n\n#### Progress Bar Pattern:\n- Flex layout bar container\n- Inner fill div with percentage width\n- Smooth transitions (300ms)\n- Color theming\n\n### Key Technical Details\n\n**Stack:**\n- React 19.2, React Router 7.6, Redux Toolkit 2.11\n- Playwright 1.52 with Replay.io 5.0\n- Netlify Functions (serverless)\n- Neon PostgreSQL\n\n**State Management:**\n- Redux slices for: auth, teams, issues, cycles, etc.\n- Async thunks for API calls\n- Local component state for UI (dropdowns, modals, selections)\n\n**API Pattern:**\n- Bearer token authentication (Authorization header)\n- Query parameters for filtering (teamId, cycleId)\n- JSON request/response bodies\n- Error responses with HTTP status codes\n\n**Testing Pattern:**\n- API-based login before each test\n- localStorage token storage\n- Absolute timeouts with specific element checks\n- Data-testid for element selection\n- API calls to fetch expected data for assertions\n\n---\n\n**Absolute file paths for reference:**\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleList.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleDetail.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateCycle.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/BurndownChart.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/ActiveCycle.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycles.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycle-issues.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/cycle-list.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/cycle-detail.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/create-issue-modal-cycles-dates.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueRow.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/App.tsx`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad34d23f2b63e2903 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 81634\ntool_uses: 35\nduration_ms: 69542</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ee9f87d-051a-4e97-9b18-73c5fcdfaaeb","uuid":"1dc2a9c1-c1f8-4b73-939d-2accd8aa00d2","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the linear clone app in the /repo/apps/ directory. I need to understand:\n1. What's the app directory name?\n2. What's the overall structure (pages, components, netlify functions)?\n3. Find all cycle-related components, pages, and API endpoints\n4. Find all burndown chart related components\n5. Find existing test files to understand patterns\n6. Read the test spec file (docs/tests.md or similar) for cycle and burndown chart test entries\n7. Read the playwright config\n8. Read the database schema/seed files\n9. Read any shared UI components (modals, buttons) used in cycles\n\nBe very thorough - read the actual source code of cycle-related components, burndown chart components, and API endpoints.","agentId":"ad34d23f2b63e2903","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Linear Clone App - Complete Exploration Summary\n\n### 1. App Directory Name\n**`/repo/apps/LinearClone`** - The main application directory\n\n### 2. Overall Structure\n\nThe app follows a standard React + Redux + Netlify Functions architecture:\n\n**Key directories:**\n- **`src/`** - Frontend React application\n  - **`pages/`** - Top-level page components (routing targets)\n  - **`components/`** - Reusable UI components\n  - **`slices/`** - Redux state management\n- **`netlify/functions/`** - Serverless API endpoints\n- **`tests/`** - Playwright end-to-end tests\n- **`scripts/`** - Database schema and seed utilities\n- **`docs/tests.md`** - Comprehensive test specification document\n- **`playwright.config.ts`** - Test configuration with Replay.io integration\n- **`public/`** - Static assets\n\n### 3. Cycle-Related Components, Pages, and API Endpoints\n\n#### Frontend Pages:\n- **`src/pages/ActiveCycle.tsx`** - Main cycles page at `/team/:teamId/cycles` route\n  - Manages cycle list and detail view toggling\n  - Handles cycle creation via modal\n  - Dispatches Redux actions for cycle fetching and selection\n\n#### Components:\n- **`src/components/CycleList.tsx`** - Displays paginated list of cycles with:\n  - Cycle name, date range, progress bar, issue count\n  - Active cycle highlighting with visual badge\n  - Click to navigate to detail view\n- **`src/components/CycleDetail.tsx`** - Shows detailed cycle view with:\n  - Cycle name, date range, progress statistics (total, completed, in progress, remaining)\n  - Progress bar with percentage\n  - Burndown chart integration\n  - Issue list with grouping (status, priority, assignee, project, label)\n  - Sorting options (priority, created, updated, status)\n  - Status filtering\n  - Bulk issue selection and status updates\n  - All filtering/sorting state stored in Redux\n- **`src/components/CreateCycle.tsx`** - Modal for creating new cycles with:\n  - Name, start date, end date input fields\n  - Form validation (required fields, end date > start date)\n  - Submit button with loading state\n  - Escape key and overlay click to close\n\n#### Redux State Management:\n- **`src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`** - Comprehensive state management:\n  - `CycleSummary` interface: id, name, startDate, endDate, teamId, issueCount, doneCount, inProgressCount, isActive\n  - `CycleIssue` interface: extends Issue with cycleName\n  - `CycleDetail` interface: id, name, startDate, endDate, teamId\n  - `BurndownEntry` interface: date, count\n  - Async thunks:\n    - `fetchCycles(teamId)` - GET `/api/cycles?teamId={teamId}`\n    - `fetchCycleIssues(cycleId)` - GET `/api/cycle-issues?cycleId={cycleId}`\n    - `createCycle(teamId, name, startDate, endDate)` - POST `/api/cycles`\n  - Reducers: setCycleGroupBy, setCycleSortBy, toggleCycleIssueSelection, selectCycleGroupIssues, clearCycleSelection, setSelectedCycleId\n  - State properties: cycles[], loading, error, selectedCycleId, cycleDetail, cycleIssues[], cycleMembers[], burndown[], detailLoading, detailError, groupBy, sortBy, selectedIds[]\n\n#### API Endpoints:\n- **`netlify/functions/cycles.ts`** - GET/POST cycles\n  - **GET** `/api/cycles?teamId={teamId}` - Returns list of cycles with stats, determines active cycle based on current date\n  - **POST** `/api/cycles` - Creates new cycle (requires teamId, name, startDate, endDate)\n  \n- **`netlify/functions/cycle-issues.ts`** - GET cycle details with issues and burndown\n  - **GET** `/api/cycle-issues?cycleId={cycleId}` - Returns cycle info, issues in cycle, team members, and burndown data\n  - Fetches activity log entries where status changed to 'done' for burndown data\n  - Joins with labels, projects, assignees\n\n### 4. Burndown Chart Components\n\n#### Component:\n- **`src/components/BurndownChart.tsx`** - Bar chart visualization showing:\n  - Issues completed per day for the cycle duration\n  - X-axis: All dates from cycle start to end (with smart label skipping for long cycles)\n  - Y-axis: Count of issues (0 to max with even distribution)\n  - Bar heights proportional to issue count\n  - Hover tooltips with date and count\n  - Empty state message when no completions yet\n  - Responsive, scrollable for long date ranges\n\n#### Styling:\n- **`src/components/BurndownChart.css`** - Bar chart styling:\n  - Container with flex layout, overflow scrolling for long date ranges\n  - Y-axis with right-aligned labels\n  - Bars with accent color, smooth height transitions\n  - Rounded bar tops, semi-transparent hover effect\n\n#### Data Flow:\n- BurndownEntry[] fetched from `/api/cycle-issues` endpoint\n- Data points computed from activity log (field='status', new_value='done')\n- Dates within cycle range rendered, others show 0 height\n\n### 5. Existing Test Files (Playwright)\n\nTests follow consistent patterns with helper functions:\n\n**Cycle-Related Tests:**\n- **`tests/cycle-list.spec.ts`** (6 tests)\n  - Renders all cycles with name, date range, progress bar, issue count\n  - Active cycle highlighted with badge and CSS class\n  - Clicking cycle navigates to detail\n  - Empty state when no cycles\n  - Progress bar accuracy\n  - Updates when new cycle created\n  - Switching between cycles in list\n\n- **`tests/cycle-detail.spec.ts`** (8 tests)\n  - Renders cycle name and date range\n  - Shows progress stats (total, completed, in progress, remaining)\n  - Shows progress bar with percentage\n  - Displays filtered issue list\n  - Clicking issue navigates to detail page\n  - Supports grouping by status/priority/assignee\n  - Supports sorting\n  - Supports filtering by status\n  - Supports bulk actions (status change)\n  - Updates stats when issue status changes\n  - Renders correctly for cycle with no issues\n\n- **`tests/create-issue-modal-cycles-dates.spec.ts`** (3+ cycle-related tests)\n  - Cycle dropdown shows team's cycles\n  - Selecting a cycle\n  - Updating cycles when team changes\n\n**Test Pattern:**\n- Login via API and store token in localStorage\n- Use API helpers to fetch teams and cycles\n- Navigate to pages with team/cycle IDs\n- Verify UI with data-testid selectors\n- Test interactions and state changes\n- Timeouts: 30s for page loads, 10s for modals, 15s for interactions\n\n### 6. Test Specification File\n\n**`docs/tests.md`** (48,000+ tokens) contains:\n- Comprehensive test entries for Active Cycle page (section starting line ~1450)\n- Tests cover:\n  - Cycle list rendering and interactions\n  - Cycle detail views\n  - Progress statistics\n  - Burndown chart display\n  - Cycle creation modal\n  - Form validation\n  - Issue list filtering, grouping, sorting, bulk actions\n  - Empty states\n  - Data persistence\n\n**Burndown Chart Test Entries (lines ~1589-1614):**\n- \"Burndown chart displays completion data correctly\"\n- \"Burndown chart shows correct date range\"\n- \"Burndown chart updates in real-time\"\n- \"Burndown chart shows empty state\"\n- \"Burndown chart y-axis scales proportionally\"\n- \"Burndown chart handles long date ranges\"\n\n### 7. Playwright Configuration\n\n**`playwright.config.ts`:**\n- Test timeout: 60 seconds\n- Expect timeout: 10 seconds\n- Fully parallel execution\n- Retry: 0\n- Reporters: Replay.io, JSON results, HTML report\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Action timeout: 15 seconds\n- Uses `@replayio/playwright` for browser recording\n\n### 8. Database Schema and Seed Files\n\n**`scripts/schema.ts`** - Creates PostgreSQL tables:\n- **cycles** table:\n  - id (UUID, PK)\n  - name (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n  - start_date (DATE, NOT NULL)\n  - end_date (DATE, NOT NULL)\n  - team_id (UUID, FK to teams)\n  - status (TEXT, DEFAULT 'active')\n  - Index: idx_cycles_team_id\n\n- **issues** table (extended):\n  - cycle_id (UUID, FK to cycles, nullable)\n  - parent_id (UUID, self-referencing)\n  - Index: idx_issues_cycle_id\n\n- **activity** table - For burndown tracking:\n  - id, issue_id (FK), member_id (FK), action, field, new_value, created_at\n  - Index: idx_activity_issue_id\n\n**`scripts/seed-db.ts`** - Seeds test data:\n- Creates 3 members: Alice (admin), Bob, Carol\n- Creates 2 teams: Engineering (ENG), Design (DES)\n- Creates 1 cycle: \"Sprint 12\" (2026-03-10 to 2026-03-24, active)\n- Creates 8 issues for ENG team with various statuses and assignments\n- Creates 3 issues for DES team\n- Issues assigned to cycle (mostly to Sprint 12)\n- Labels created (Bug, Feature, Improvement, Documentation)\n- Notifications seeded\n\n### 9. Shared UI Components Used in Cycles\n\n#### IssueRow Component (`src/components/IssueRow.tsx`):\n- **Shared across:** Cycle detail, team issues, my issues pages\n- **Features:**\n  - Issue checkbox with selection handling\n  - Status icon (visual indicator by status)\n  - Priority icon\n  - Issue identifier and title\n  - Assignee avatar/initials\n  - Labels display\n  - Due date (if present)\n  - Status dropdown for inline status change\n  - Click to navigate to issue detail\n- **Exports:** STATUS_CONFIG, STATUS_ORDER, StatusIcon, PriorityIcon (used in CycleDetail)\n- **Test IDs:** issue-row-{id}, issue-identifier-{id}, issue-title-{id}, issue-checkbox-{id}, issue-status-btn-{id}\n\n#### Modal Patterns:\n- **CreateCycle.tsx** uses modal overlay pattern:\n  - Fixed overlay with backdrop blur\n  - Centered modal box with shadow\n  - Click outside to close\n  - Escape key handling\n  - Disabled submit button during submission\n\n#### Button Components:\n- All use standard CSS classes with:\n  - Hover states\n  - Disabled states (opacity reduction)\n  - Transition animations (150ms)\n  - Color theming via CSS variables (--color-accent, --color-border, --color-text-*)\n\n#### Dropdown Patterns:\n- Positioned dropdowns with click-outside detection\n- useRef + useEffect for outside click handling\n- Toggle state management\n- Close on selection\n\n#### Progress Bar Pattern:\n- Flex layout bar container\n- Inner fill div with percentage width\n- Smooth transitions (300ms)\n- Color theming\n\n### Key Technical Details\n\n**Stack:**\n- React 19.2, React Router 7.6, Redux Toolkit 2.11\n- Playwright 1.52 with Replay.io 5.0\n- Netlify Functions (serverless)\n- Neon PostgreSQL\n\n**State Management:**\n- Redux slices for: auth, teams, issues, cycles, etc.\n- Async thunks for API calls\n- Local component state for UI (dropdowns, modals, selections)\n\n**API Pattern:**\n- Bearer token authentication (Authorization header)\n- Query parameters for filtering (teamId, cycleId)\n- JSON request/response bodies\n- Error responses with HTTP status codes\n\n**Testing Pattern:**\n- API-based login before each test\n- localStorage token storage\n- Absolute timeouts with specific element checks\n- Data-testid for element selection\n- API calls to fetch expected data for assertions\n\n---\n\n**Absolute file paths for reference:**\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleList.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleDetail.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateCycle.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/BurndownChart.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/ActiveCycle.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycles.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycle-issues.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/cycle-list.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/cycle-detail.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/create-issue-modal-cycles-dates.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueRow.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/App.tsx`"}],"totalDurationMs":69542,"totalTokens":81634,"totalToolUseCount":35,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":77792,"output_tokens":3383,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":459},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
